From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BipAgents <patches@bipagents.local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:41:06 +0100
Subject: MCP calls carry their session to a server that asks (call_context)

A server whose config says call_context: true gets, in each tools/call's _meta, the Hermes session the call comes
from (hermes-agent/session_id). A server serving several conversations of one agent at once (BipAgents' bridge: a
person's conversation and several background tasks) then tells their calls apart instead of guessing from the last
tool started. Off by default: no other server ever sees a session id.

BipAgents patch, documented in hermes/patches/README.md of the BipAgents repository.

Bip-Patch: 0028-mcp-call-context-session
